# Alice upstream fork

This workspace extends **[pmbstyle/alice](https://github.com/pmbstyle/alice)** but maintains a **fork** because upstream is unlikely to adopt opinionated security and privacy changes (e.g. narrowing IPC / HTTP bridges, localhost-only listeners, stricter update/binary provenance).

## Principles for the agent

- Prefer **minimal, reviewable diffs** that stay mergeable with upstream; isolate invasive changes behind flags or small modules when possible.
- When fixing bugs, consider whether the fix can be **contributed upstream** as a separate PR (narrow scope, no controversial defaults).
- Before large merges from upstream, identify files we intentionally diverged on and **merge or rebase carefully** (resolve conflicts in favor of documented local policy unless upstream clearly fixes a bug we need).

## Update workflow (human / Git)

Use two remotes on the fork clone:

- **`origin`** → your fork (push destination).
- **`upstream`** → `https://github.com/pmbstyle/alice.git` (read-only updates).

One-time setup:

```bash
git remote add upstream https://github.com/pmbstyle/alice.git   # if not already added
git fetch upstream
```

Recommended rhythm (merge upstream into a branch first, then into `main`):

```bash
git fetch upstream
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b merge-upstream-$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
git merge upstream/main
# resolve conflicts (expect electron/, vite.config.ts, IPC paths, deps)
# run tests / build
git checkout main
git merge merge-upstream-$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
git push origin main
git tag merge-upstream-$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
git push origin merge-upstream-$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
```

Simpler alternative (merge directly on `main`):

```bash
git fetch upstream
git checkout main
git merge upstream/main
# resolve conflicts, test, then:
git push origin main
```

Prefer **`merge`** over **`rebase`** on shared `main` unless you accept rewriting published history. Use **`git rebase upstream/main`** only on private branches.

Before integrating: skim **`git log upstream/main`** for changes touching areas we diverged (Electron preload/main, IPC, build scripts). After merge: run tests/build.

**Conflict hotspots:** `electron/`, `vite.config.ts`, IPC-heavy paths, dependency bumps — resolve using documented local policy; note intentional divergence in commits or short comments.

**Upstream-friendly fixes:** narrow bugfixes can be contributed as PRs to **`pmbstyle/Alice`** from a branch based on **`upstream/main`**; keep the fork’s hardening separate.

## Other forks

The public fork network is **small** (~30 forks, mostly zero stars). Do **not** assume another fork is a second “product line” worth tracking unless you verify it has commits **ahead** of `pmbstyle/Alice` and recent activity. Default source of “goodness” remains **`upstream`** plus upstream issues/releases.
